Declare the glibc and kernel-headers trampoline repos reproducible so they can use the
repo contents cache.

Both only render a checked-in BUILD template, so they are trivially reproducible. Upstream
already marks the heavier llvm repos reproducible (see
https://github.com/hermeticbuild/hermetic-llvm/pull/603) but missed these two.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/kernel/extension/kernel_headers.bzl b/kernel/extension/kernel_headers.bzl
index 402cde8..b130ca4 100644
--- a/kernel/extension/kernel_headers.bzl
+++ b/kernel/extension/kernel_headers.bzl
@@ -5,6 +5,12 @@ def _kernel_headers_trampoline_repository_impl(repository_ctx):
     repository_ctx.template("BUILD.bazel", repository_ctx.attr._build_file)
     repository_ctx.file("linux_kernel_version_map.bzl", repository_ctx.attr.version_map)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks repository_ctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(repository_ctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return repository_ctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 _kernel_headers_trampoline_repository = repository_rule(
     implementation = _kernel_headers_trampoline_repository_impl,
     attrs = {
